{"name":"Hello Summer","hex":"#55bbff","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hello","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["A greeting (salutation) said when meeting someone or acknowledging someone’s arrival or presence.","A greeting used when answering the telephone."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["\"Hello!\" or an equivalent greeting."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hello"},{"term":"summer","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One of four seasons, traditionally the second, marked by the longest and typically hottest days of the year due to the inclination of the Earth and thermal lag. Typically regarded as spanning  either the period between the summer solstice to the autumnal equinox, or the months of June, July, and August in the Northern Hemisphere and the months of December, January and February in the Southern Hemisphere.","year; used to give the age of a person, usually a young one."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To spend the summer, as in a particular place on holiday."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/summer"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hello Summer (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Hello Summer\" is a song recorded by American country music singer Danielle Bradbery for her second studio album, I Don't Believe We've Met (2017). The song was written by Thomas Rhett, Rhett Akins, and Jaren Johnston as well as the track's producer, Julian Bunetta. A solo version by Bradbery was released digitally through Big Machine Records as the album's second promotional single on September 22, 2017. In 2018, \"Hello Summer\" was re-recorded as a duet with one of its co-writers, Thomas Rhett, and released under the title \"Goodbye Summer\" as the album's third official radio single."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/33/Danielle_Bradbery_-_Hello_Summer_%28single_cover%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hello_Summer_(song)","wikidata":"Q60744575"},{"title":"Hello","blocks":[{"text":"Hello is a salutation or greeting in the English language. It is first attested in writing from 1826."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/TelephoneHelloNellie.jpg/330px-TelephoneHelloNellie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hello","wikidata":"Q98815142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/33/Danielle_Bradbery_-_Hello_Summer_%28single_cover%29.jpg/250px-Danielle_Bradbery_-_Hello_Summer_%28single_cover%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/33/Danielle_Bradbery_-_Hello_Summer_%28single_cover%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/33/Danielle_Bradbery_-_Hello_Summer_%28single_cover%29.jpg/250px-Danielle_Bradbery_-_Hello_Summer_%28single_cover%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADanielle_Bradbery_-_Hello_Summer_(single_cover).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/ff/Danielle_Bradbery_-_Goodbye_Summer_%28single_cover%29.jpg/250px-Danielle_Bradbery_-_Goodbye_Summer_%28single_cover%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/ff/Danielle_Bradbery_-_Goodbye_Summer_%28single_cover%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/ff/Danielle_Bradbery_-_Goodbye_Summer_%28single_cover%29.jpg/250px-Danielle_Bradbery_-_Goodbye_Summer_%28single_cover%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.o